=======
  "notes": "Charging policy of each cell is read from the batch file's policy_readable field (e.g. 3.6C(80%)-3.6C). The two batch files present cover two of the three batches of the study; cell specification is not in Raw_Dataset. Cell and test conditions read from the Severson et al. Methods section (fetched from the MIT-hosted PDF); the dataset itself ships no documentation. Charge-rate maximum is taken across all locally available cell policies, not the modal policy; the discharge rate is independently stated as 4C in the paper Methods. Charging profile: the charge rate differs between cells but is fixed within each cell. The full text of the paper was supplied by the user and read in full: it confirms the A123 APR18650M1A cell (1.1 Ah, 3.3 V), the 124-cell total over three batches (this record holds 94 from two of them), 30 C, one- and two-step 0-80% SOC charging policies of 3.6C to 6C (8C/4C only in the diagnostic experiments of Fig. 4), a uniform 1C CC-CV charge from 80% to 100% to 3.6 V with C/50 cut-off, and a 4C CC-CV discharge to 2.0 V with C/50 cut-off. Rate combinations: the charge is multi-stage, not a single CC-CV rate, so none are listed; the 4C discharge is the same for all cells. Rate groups: the multi-stage CC-CV charge (a different policy per cell, no single rate) against the 4C CC-CV discharge, listed as a group with no charge rates."
